From: Nolan Cotter <186326284+NolanCotter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:14:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] d3d12_xs: route console list slot 139 (Reset) to PC
 slot 10
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pipodi measured the retail title calling console list slot 139 with
(allocator proxy, pso) before recording — Reset, at PC slot 10. Map it
and unwrap the allocator (and a pipeline state the same way); the
unwrap now keys on the PC slot so console-10 and console-139 both land
on the real Reset.

xs_proxy_mock: PASS under Wine

Generated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)

Co-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 docs/d3d12_xs_console_abi.md      | 1 +
 runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/d3d12_xs_console_abi.md b/docs/d3d12_xs_console_abi.md
index 604eb0e1f..e1ec05fc7 100644
--- a/docs/d3d12_xs_console_abi.md
+++ b/docs/d3d12_xs_console_abi.md
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@ end; on a full buffer they call the vtable method the record stands for (Package
 | 80 | `ExecuteIndirect` | Sibling layer (note: the package measured slot 80 as a console-only call, a `Dispatch`-with-extra-word shape; slot assignments past 61 differ between the two sources — unconfirmed) |
 | 83 | `CopyTextureRegionX` (older layout) | Sibling layer; the package measured a `CopyTextureRegion`-shaped call at slot 85 — consistent with the newer layout (+2) |
 | 108 | `ResolveSubresourceRegion` | Sibling layer |
+| 139 | `Reset(allocator, pso)` → PC slot 10 | **Measured here**: retail 1.0.2.1 (Pipodi) — the title creates a list, `Close`s at slot 9, then calls 139 with `(allocator proxy, 0)` before recording; the proxy unwraps the allocator and forwards to PC `Reset` |
 | 146 | enhanced `Barrier` | **Confirmed here**: Package (console slot 146 takes one `D3D12_BARRIER_GROUP`; PC equivalent is GCL7 slot 80) |
 | 148 | `AllocateUploadMemory` `(size, alignment)`; the returned CPU pointer is the GPU address in unified memory | Package + sibling layer |
 
diff --git a/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp b/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp
index 72da24e4e..69d84bb73 100644
--- a/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp
+++ b/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.cpp
@@ -1827,6 +1827,7 @@ constexpr unsigned kConsoleClearDepthStencilView = 51;
 constexpr unsigned kConsoleClearRenderTargetView = 52;
 constexpr unsigned kConsoleClearUavUint = 53;
 constexpr unsigned kConsoleClearUavFloat = 54;
+constexpr unsigned kConsoleReset = 139;
 constexpr unsigned kConsoleBarrier = 146;
 constexpr unsigned kConsoleAllocateUpload = 148;
 
@@ -1837,6 +1838,7 @@ constexpr unsigned console_to_pc_list_slot(unsigned slot) {
     if (slot == 60) return 58;                 // EndEvent (no console SetMarker/BeginEvent)
     if (slot == 61) return 59;                 // ExecuteIndirect (Package)
     if (slot == kConsoleBarrier) return 80;    // D3D12_BARRIER_GROUP (Package; PC GCL7)
+    if (slot == kConsoleReset) return 10;      // Reset(allocator, pso): measured on the retail title (Pipodi)
     return kListNotForwarded;
 }
 
@@ -2019,9 +2021,12 @@ std::uint64_t WINAPI list_slot(ListProxy* self, std::uint64_t a1, std::uint64_t
                                                      std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t,
                                                      std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t);
             auto** const real_vtable = *reinterpret_cast<void***>(self->real);
-            if constexpr (Slot == 10) {
-                // Reset(allocator, pso): the title hands its allocator proxy; the real list takes the real one.
+            if constexpr (pc == 10) {
+                // Reset(allocator, pso) — console 10, and 139 as the retail title calls it: the title hands its
+                // allocator proxy; the real list takes the real one (and a wrapped pipeline state, if that ever
+                // exists, the same way).
                 a1 = unwrap_object(a1);
+                a2 = unwrap_object(a2);
             } else if constexpr (Slot == kConsoleExecuteBundle) {
                 a1 = unwrap_object(a1);  // the bundle is a list proxy too
             } else if constexpr (Slot >= 41 && Slot <= 46) {
